hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15567","Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: My brother al-Hakam ibn al-Muttalib narrated to me, from his father, from Quhayd ibn Mutarrif al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked by an asker: If an aggressor attacks me, and he ordered him to forbid him three times. He said: If he refuses, then he ordered him to fight him. He said: How about us? He said: If he kills you, you are in Paradise, and if you kill him, he is in the Fire."
"15568","Yaqub narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his brother al-Hakam ibn al-Muttalib, from his father, from Quhayd al-Ghifari, he said: An asker asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If an aggressor attacks me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remind him, and he ordered him to remind him three times. If he refuses, then fight him. If he kills you, you are in Paradise, and if you kill him, he is in the Fire."
